                            {
                                "example_id": "28568e48-05d4-4182-8e96-5fa9cf78b1a5",
                                "sense_id": "53beae63-dd4c-30ed-b3b0-33026e5e5bc3",
                                "text": "“What are ye for?” he shouted. “T’ maister’s down i’ t’ fowld. Go round by th’ end o’ t’ laith, if ye went to spake to him.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec655b70-5917-4810-b248-e819c5f9cf27",
                                "sense_id": "53beae63-dd4c-30ed-b3b0-33026e5e5bc3",
                                "text": "Six quarters of wheat were held at Thomas Roger's house, and in laiths outside Bootham and Micklegate Bar he had store of wheat, rye, barley, beans and peas, totalling £21 6s 8d which represented about a quarter of his assets."
